{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1557724-paths-and-personalities-2ed","id":1557724,"title":"Paths and Personalities 2ed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-18T06:33:27-08:00","id":1557724,"title":"Paths and Personalities 2ed","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Certain personalities seem more drawn to a path than others, but is there any confirmation whether anyone can awaken to any path?<br /> <br /> Like a somewhat dour and solitary person HAS to be Moros? Can't they be an unusually reflective Acanthus? Or a person that prizes intellectual pursuits over social interaction... Are those always Mastigos? A non dogmatic, non religious Obrimos?<br /> <br /> I tried a bit with Tome of the Watchtowers, but it seems to me that it only reinforces stereotypes of each path.<br /> <br /> So I think the main question is: does a path make you have a certain personality, or does having certain personality traits make you have the path?<br /> <br /> Looking for some guidance.<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T08:02:59-08:00","id":1557726,"title":"","content":"Signs of sorcery, if i remember correctly, stetes that the corresponding watchtowers activates when they sense a right kind of soul","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T08:24:00-08:00","id":1557727,"title":"","content":"Selection bias is absolutely a factor, as are the influence of the powers and symbolic associations of the Path after Awakening, and Internal metamorphic Awakenings can alter the personality among other things, but no, theoretically there's nothing stopping any of the Watchtowers from drawing anybody with the other two traits necessary for Awakening into a Mystery Play.<br /> <br /> The sample Forge Master from Legacies: the Ancient specifically tries to act differently whenever anybody tries to stereotype him by his race, Legacy, or profession, and is really peeved that having his leg crushed in the car accident that led to his Awakening in a way that resists magical healing means he embodies a mythic archetype.<br /> <br /> People have gone over this before, but essentially the type of person who is likely to succeed at the trials of a given Watchtower and gains the basic powers of its Path typically has some of the associated outlook going into and/or coming out of the Awakening.<br /> <br /> To draw some analogies to other gamelines:<br /> <br /> Any Horror can theoretically Devour any deep dreamer to turn them into a Beast, but the type of dreamer who is <i>likely</i> to be Devoured by a Leviathan with a Hunger for Ruin is one who has deep-rooted fears about the ocean and destruction and recognizes themselves in those fears.<br /> <br /> Any Fae can theoretically turn any mortal into a changeling, but the Fae who wants or needs flames to light their ballroom is <i>likely</i> to gather up people with literally or metaphorically luminous qualities, and those who manage to escape are often people who can put their new magical abilities in that vein to best use.<br /> <br /> Any vampire can theoretically turn any mortal into a vampire, but the powers and banes of a given Clan and/or bloodline put adaptational pressures on their members in favor of those who can make the most of them and the Embrace is a sufficiently major investment of resources that doing it on purpose is not done lightly or without at least a little bit of vetting to ensure that the new childe is <i>likely</i> to survive.<br /> <br /> <br /> To further add: The Moros are historically <i>not</i> a dour Path, contrary to common expectations of a group of people with power over Death, non-religious Obrimos are well-established, and the Acanthus stereotype of flightiness was, in the leadup to 2e, directly compared to the metaphor of swans seeming to be serene and graceful while kicking frantically below the surface.<br /> <br /> The Paths give a category of symbolism along with their freer use of two Arcana, and that incentivizes the direction of their members' magical personae toward certain umbrellas, but the way Shadow Names work allows you to have that have no overlap with your character's mundane persona \u2014 it's a matter of acting and expression as much as who they are as a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T08:35:39-08:00","id":1557728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1557724-paths-and-personalities-2ed#post1557724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certain personalities seem more drawn to a path than others, but is there any confirmation whether anyone can awaken to any path?</div> </div> </div> </div>Over the whole course of the game's fiction, I think one will find a basis for the point that the personalities within the Paths can be fairly diverse. Like, dour and solitary describes to a tee that one Acanthus in the Ebon Noose in First Edition, at least as I recall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ibeaumanior</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A non dogmatic, non religious Obrimos?</div> </div> </div> </div>That one's easy. Even the description of Awakening in the Second Edition core gives the example of a mathematician who sees her side of the Supernal in the form of data for statistical models, and the overall outline includes the likes of physicists and programmers. The heart of the Obrimos is reality as an ordered system, and while that frequently and traditionally comes in the form of the order of a divine will, it lends itself quite organically as a rational materialist sequence. Signs of Sorcery might use references to angelology to describe the Arcana, but that can be seen as more poetic than literal in a way that a give Obrimos might still dispense with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ibeaumanior</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think the main question is: does a path make you have a certain personality, or does having certain personality traits make you have the path?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's probably varying degrees of both for different mages. At the furthest extremes of the spectrum are probably people who find the Awakening a profound enough experience that it heavily changes their priorities and worldview in line of the symbols they saw in it and capabilities they gain from it, and those people who were very strong-willed and opinionated in a manner that would not adhere to the Path's traditional mythos, but nevertheless have the pattern of their inquiring mind and the circumstances of their confrontation with the Lie resonate with a specific Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T09:25:44-08:00","id":1557730,"title":"","content":"In my mind, the stereotypes are a combination of tendencies of the people who sign the Watchtowers and how they interpret their symbolism: <br /> <br /> * Acanthus candidates crave freedom and will walk the thorny path to seize new hope.<br /> <br /> * Mastigos were weighted down by emotional burdens and will walk the fearsome path to master their selfhood. <br /> <br /> * Moros had a sobering confrontation with death and will walk a transforming path to refine themselves.<br /> <br /> * Obrimos see higher purpose and potential in everything, and will walk the formidable path to realize it.<br /> <br /> * Thyrsus have a powerful intuitive understanding of their place in their ecosystem and will walk the ecstatic path of adaptation.<br /> <br /> All that matters is you resonated enough to hear the call of the Watchtower. An Acanthus might think seizing hope means being spontaneous and improvisational, another might think it's all about forethought and planning, yet another might decide to take a middle road, and so on. They might even change their perspective during their careers, but that core resonance is still there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T10:56:48-08:00","id":1557732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1557724-paths-and-personalities-2ed?p=1557726#post1557726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Signs of sorcery, if i remember correctly, stetes that the corresponding watchtowers activates when they sense a right kind of soul</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the right kind of soul for each watchtower? Do we have a detailed pre-awakening conditions that should make it clear where do you end up &quot;<i>Ahhh, Jack is or has a XXXX, therefore if he awakens he clearly will be a YYYY&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T11:09:12-08:00","id":1557733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1557724-paths-and-personalities-2ed?p=1557732#post1557732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the right kind of soul for each watchtower? Do we have a detailed pre-awakening conditions that should make it clear where do you end up &quot;<i>Ahhh, Jack is or has a XXXX, therefore if he awakens he clearly will be a YYYY&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Same book Neos is referencing:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Signs of Sorcery, p130, &quot;The Intercession of a Watchtower&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Orders debate how much the stereotypes of mages belonging to each Path come from the Watchtower only choosing people who fit with that Path, how much comes from behavior driven by access to that Path\u2019s Ruling Arcana and Supernal World, and how much might be natural selection of only some Prospects succeeding at the challenges posed by that Path\u2019s Awakenings. No one has a definitive answer, and among Alethians it resembles the nature/nurture question for biologists. It\u2019s even difficult to say whether the final confrontation with the Lie that triggers Awakening must fit with the Path-to-be\u2019s Symbolism because, if it didn\u2019t, it will as soon as the Awakening begins and the newly Lucid Prospect\u2019s world fills with symbols.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a mystery. You figure it out for your individual table and/or character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-22T22:53:13-08:00","id":1557850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1557724-paths-and-personalities-2ed?p=1557726#post1557726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Signs of sorcery, if i remember correctly, stetes that the corresponding watchtowers activates when they sense a right kind of soul</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would make sense, as they're referred to specifically as Paths.<br /> <br /> <br /> Pandemonium, for example, is the Path of Transgression and Punishment, so mages who draw power from there have to be rebellious or vengeful if they want to get the most benefit out of their respective Watchtower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T05:09:20-08:00","id":1557853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1557724-paths-and-personalities-2ed?p=1557850#post1557850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which would make sense, as they're referred to specifically as Paths.<br /> <br /> <br /> Pandemonium, for example, is the Path of Transgression and Punishment, so mages who draw power from there have to be rebellious or vengeful if they want to get the most benefit out of their respective Watchtower.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What would people have to be to get more of the other four paths benefits?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T12:13:20-08:00","id":1557862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1557724-paths-and-personalities-2ed?p=1557853#post1557853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would people have to be to get more of the other four paths benefits?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I had to make a guess? I'd probably suggest the following:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Acanthus</b> - <i>Choice and Consequences:</i> so people who crave total freedom, and are willing to accept the risks that come with it.<br /> <br /> <b>Thyrsus</b> - <i>Boundaries and Intercession:</i> so people who understand how things are meant to work, and when something is disrupting that natural order.<br /> <br /> <b>Obrimos</b> - <i>Power and Command:</i> so people who desire authority over others. I've noticed all the Chronicle splats seem to feature their own version of such.<br /> <br /> <b>Moros</b> - <i>Permanence and Transition:</i> I admit, I'm having a hard time coming up with a suggestion for this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-16T00:50:06-08:00","id":1558349,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1557724-paths-and-personalities-2ed?p=1557850#post1557850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pandemonium, for example, is the Path of Transgression and Punishment, so mages who draw power from there have to be rebellious or vengeful if they want to get the most benefit out of their respective Watchtower.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor correction: it's Transgression and <i>Confrontation</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1557724-paths-and-personalities-2ed?p=1557862#post1557862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Obrimos</b> - <i>Power and Command:</i> so people who desire authority over others. I've noticed all the Chronicle splats seem to feature their own version of such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree with this, but I'd extend it to authority over <i>anything</i>. The key issue for the Obrimos is being able to speak and be obeyed. If you command the lock to open, then it should open. If you tell the fire not to burn, then it should not burn. If you call for lightning to strike, then it should strike. As others have noted, the mechanism of authority is not specified: I have authority over this door, because I can turn the handle and pull it open, because I know how doors work. Authority arises from knowledge or gnosis; it isn't merely granted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1557724-paths-and-personalities-2ed?p=1557862#post1557862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Moros</b> - <i>Permanence and Transition:</i> I admit, I'm having a hard time coming up with a suggestion for this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think of Moros in terms of componentization: people who reflexively break things down into parts. In one sense, this can be visionary: you see a tree, but he sees a grand table; you see an open plain, he sees a future city; you see a sinner, but he sees a saint in the making. In another sense, this can be viscerally disturbing: you see a person, but he sees meat and bones; you see a bank, but he sees construction materials; you see a good man, but he sees someone who could fall. In both cases, it's the recognition that the thing is not just the thing, but made of other things which can be changed or repurposed.<br /> <br /> I could boil down each of the Paths into a thesis statement like so: That you always have a choice. That any boundary can be broken. That we are all <s>star</s>magic stuff. That every lock has a key. That every thing has a place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1557724-paths-and-personalities-2ed#post1557724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bLike a somewhat dour and solitary person HAS to be Moros? Can't they be an unusually reflective Acanthus? Or a person that prizes intellectual pursuits over social interaction... Are those always Mastigos? A non dogmatic, non religious Obrimos?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>So, here's a non-dour, non-solitary Moros concept: an interior decorator. He takes clients and transforms their homes as cheaply as possible, rearranging their spaces, selecting artwork and matching furniture, carefully delineating a home office from the living room, making sure that the household can hear a call from the kitchen, and so on. He rarely adds to the home; he prefers to use what's already there, maybe dressing it up a little in different-colored coverings, something that catches the light better, or worse, and so on. In his Shadow life, he provides the same service to Sancta, and knows a little Prime to help clarify good ritual or oblation spaces, encourage different kinds of tass, and so on. And he can only do a good job of this by having constant, productive conversations with the residents of the places he's reassembling.<br /> <br /> Here's a dour and solitary Acanthus concept: the Cassandra. During his Awakening, he was presented with a very specific vision of the future, the usual terrible ending for the Consilium or whatever. But he has no political savvy, no one else has been able to duplicate his prediction, and his dogged pursuit of trying to persuade powerbrokers into derailing disaster has won him no friends. So now he's the Consilium grump: friendless, predictable, dismissable. A standard NPC archetype, really, and Chekov demands that his doomsaying is painfully correct.<br /> <br /> Here's an Obrimos who prizes intellectual pursuits over social interaction: the Gospel writer. He is obsessed with writing the perfect story that will trigger an Awakening: he believes that if he finds the perfect arrangement of words, plots, dialogues, and so on, then any reader will Awaken upon finishing the tale. Sure, it'd help if he actually went and talked to people to see what kinds of stories they find inspiring, but he has his opinions and read his fair share of good writing, so he thinks he's got all the puzzle pieces: the task is simply to fit them together. If you find yourself in his office, the sheer quantity of red string on corkboard will bedazzle you, from the numerology of important terms and character names to the baffling geometricity of plot structures and paragraph shapes; from pages out of a dozen sacred texts in various states of translation nailed to the walls to mathemagical analyses of his latest drafts in forty different modern languages.<br /> <br /> Here's a Mastigos concept that isn't as social as I'd intended, but I like it enough to keep: a night runner for an underground railroad. Being able to literally see the connections between people makes him uniquely suited for waltzing into a place and spiriting away people who are under threat before their attackers actually strike, sifting infiltrators from genuine victims, turning away the suspicion of various guards and hunters, creating safehouses that deflect interest, and so on, without risking Paradox. I imagine him as an Arrow, making a sacrament of the challenge of liberating the oppressed without bloodshed, a ghost in the night baffling mundane enforcers.<br /> <br /> A more social-focused Mastigos concept: the public librarian. He holds court from the checkout desk, of course, but his mental catalog of the library's offerings and easy ability to flick through the wants of Sleeper patrons makes it trivial to match an appropriate suggestion to someone's needs. He stalks the stacks occasionally, a web of sympathies linking every misplaced book to its proper place. He's the one who argues for the library's continued funding at town halls, who designs programs for patrons of every kind, who fosters a welcoming atmosphere for the entire local neighborhood: he's a bit of a public figure and acts as an implicit liaison between the magical world and the mundane. I originally imagined him as a Free Councilor, but I think that making this part of a Cryptopoly makes more sense.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}